Let $x$ be the breadth, in metres. The length is $x+3$ metres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (5,3);
\path (2.5,3) node[above] {$(x+3)\,\mathrm{m}$} (0,1.5) node[left] {$x\,\mathrm{m}$} (2.5,1.5) node {$54\,\mathrm{m}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}x(x+3)&=54\\x^{2}+3x-54&=0\\(x+9)(x-6)&=0\\x&=-9\ \text{or}\ 6\end{aligned}$
Reject $x=-9$ because a breadth must be positive. The rectangle is $6$ m by $9$ m.

Let $x$ be the base, in centimetres. The perpendicular height is $x-1$ centimetres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(5,0)--(2,3)--cycle;
\draw[black,dashed] (2,3)--(2,0);
\draw[black] (2,0.3)--(2.3,0.3)--(2.3,0);
\path (2.5,0) node[below] {$x\,\mathrm{cm}$} (2,0.8) node[right,xshift=2mm] {$(x-1)\,\mathrm{cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}\frac12 x(x-1)&=28\\x(x-1)&=56\\x^{2}-x-56&=0\\(x-8)(x+7)&=0\\x&=8\ \text{or}\ -7\end{aligned}$
Reject $x=-7$ because a base must be positive. The base is $8$ cm and the height is $7$ cm.

Let $x$ be the path width, in metres. Each outer dimension includes the path on both sides.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (8,6);
\draw[black] (1.5,1.5) rectangle (6.5,4.5);
\draw[black,<->] (6.5,3)--(8,3);
\path (4,4.5) node[below] {$8\,\mathrm{m}$} (1.5,3) node[right] {$4\,\mathrm{m}$} (7.25,3) node[above] {$x\,\mathrm{m}$} (4,6) node[above] {$(8+2x)\,\mathrm{m}$} (0,3) node[left] {$(4+2x)\,\mathrm{m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}(8+2x)(4+2x)-8\times4&=64\\4x^{2}+24x&=64\\x^{2}+6x-16&=0\\(x+8)(x-2)&=0\\x&=-8\ \text{or}\ 2\end{aligned}$
Reject $x=-8$ because a path width must be positive. The path is $2$ m wide.

Let $x$ be the shorter parallel side, in centimetres. The other parallel side is $x+4$ and the height is $x+2$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(6,0)--(4.5,3)--(1.5,3)--cycle;
\draw[black,dashed] (1.5,3)--(1.5,0);
\draw[black] (1.5,0.3)--(1.8,0.3)--(1.8,0);
\path (3,3) node[above] {$x\,\mathrm{cm}$} (3,0) node[below] {$(x+4)\,\mathrm{cm}$} (1.5,1.5) node[right] {$(x+2)\,\mathrm{cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}\frac12(x+2)(x+x+4)&=64\\(x+2)^{2}&=64\\x^{2}+4x-60&=0\\(x+10)(x-6)&=0\\x&=-10\ \text{or}\ 6\end{aligned}$
Reject $x=-10$ because a side length must be positive. The shorter parallel side is $6$ cm.
